1
00:00:05,831 --> 00:00:07,243
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,245 --> 00:00:08,725
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors. Some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,187 --> 00:00:14,660
I'd rather we never meet like this again.

4
00:00:17,427 --> 00:00:18,934
There's something I want to know.

5
00:00:22,082 --> 00:00:25,896
Is he my son?

6
00:00:28,828 --> 00:00:31,819
Is Gyeol my son?

7
00:00:36,281 --> 00:00:37,337
No.

8
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:41,673
Gyeol is my son,
and he has nothing to do with you.

9
00:00:47,354 --> 00:00:50,500
I heard Gyeol is eight.

10
00:00:51,127 --> 00:00:52,780
And we broke up eight years ago.

11
00:00:57,694 --> 00:01:01,034
Were you seeing someone else
while you were with me?

12
00:01:03,108 --> 00:01:05,726
I started seeing Heung Sik
right after we broke up.

13
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,261
Liar.

14
00:01:08,701 --> 00:01:10,860
The Han Gyu Rim I know,

15
00:01:11,845 --> 00:01:14,330
doesn't have it in her to two-time anyone,

16
00:01:14,964 --> 00:01:18,806
or the nerve to start seeing someone
the moment we broke up.

17
00:01:22,067 --> 00:01:24,093
You know me that well?

18
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:26,480
For someone who knows me so well,

19
00:01:26,568 --> 00:01:28,514
how did you get blindsided?

20
00:01:29,854 --> 00:01:31,856
After being played like that,

21
00:01:31,997 --> 00:01:34,100
you still haven't learned?

22
00:01:36,226 --> 00:01:37,979
Acting this foolish is exactly why,

23
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:40,406
you're still living such a pathetic life.

24
00:01:40,927 --> 00:01:43,287
I thought you were smart,
but you're hopeless.

25
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:47,870
Say instead that meeting someone like me
was the ruin of your whole life.

26
00:01:48,352 --> 00:01:51,619
Tell me you'll kill me on sight.
Shout at me and swear at me.

27
00:01:52,299 --> 00:01:55,613
Just stop barking up the wrong tree
and taking it out on my son.

28
00:01:56,548 --> 00:01:58,768
May I run a paternity test on Gyeol?

29
00:01:59,574 --> 00:02:00,947
Do you not understand plain words?

30
00:02:01,034 --> 00:02:02,220
A paternity test...

31
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,759
I'm asking if I may run one.

32
00:02:11,124 --> 00:02:13,176
(Wedding gift and Household Essentials)

33
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:21,914
Don't you think this is a bit much?

34
00:02:22,523 --> 00:02:24,534
How is this too much?

35
00:02:24,721 --> 00:02:26,634
For my mom, this is downright modest.

36
00:02:27,727 --> 00:02:29,902
Getting an Armes crocodile bag,

37
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:32,268
for every aunt on both sides,

38
00:02:32,328 --> 00:02:34,133
isn't exactly modest, is it?

39
00:02:35,107 --> 00:02:36,471
Then do you want to swap?

40
00:02:36,725 --> 00:02:38,694
Will you buy the apartment
instead, Gyu Yeong?

41
00:02:39,713 --> 00:02:41,045
No.

42
00:02:41,558 --> 00:02:45,017
It's just that I had no idea,

43
00:02:45,042 --> 00:02:47,431
you'd have 25 aunts.

44
00:02:57,452 --> 00:02:59,900
Your family must be very close.

45
00:03:00,094 --> 00:03:01,341
Yes, quite.

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,632
Mom.

47
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,800
Han Gyu Rim!

48
00:03:23,974 --> 00:03:25,127
Yes, Gyeol.

49
00:03:26,621 --> 00:03:28,228
Are you making burgers?

50
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:30,814
Yes.

51
00:03:32,626 --> 00:03:35,326
What did you talk with him?

52
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,700
He said sorry for calling you out
without telling me.

53
00:03:40,725 --> 00:03:43,785
See? He apologized. I told you.

54
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,673
He's a really kind, good man.

55
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:49,940
Don't ever meet that man again.

56
00:03:50,193 --> 00:03:51,200
Why?

57
00:03:51,434 --> 00:03:53,774
Just don't, because I said so.

58
00:03:53,927 --> 00:03:55,620
But why?

59
00:03:56,961 --> 00:04:00,041
Han Gyeol, why won't you listen
to me today?

60
00:04:00,167 --> 00:04:01,586
I don't like that man.

61
00:04:01,893 --> 00:04:04,760
And I don't like you going off
and meeting him either.

62
00:04:05,461 --> 00:04:07,934
Why do you dislike him so much?

63
00:04:09,448 --> 00:04:10,460
I don't know.

64
00:04:10,561 --> 00:04:12,707
I just don't. Is that enough?

65
00:04:12,734 --> 00:04:15,307
It's not. That makes no sense at all.

66
00:04:19,001 --> 00:04:20,216
Promise me.

67
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:22,387
That you'll never meet that man again.

68
00:04:24,828 --> 00:04:28,173
Han Gyeol, are you really
not going to promise me?

69
00:04:28,952 --> 00:04:31,813
Give me a reason I can accept.

70
00:04:31,868 --> 00:04:33,767
Then I won't meet him.

71
00:04:35,614 --> 00:04:38,535
And honestly, the burgers they sell,

72
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:41,698
taste much better than yours.

73
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:47,260
Who does he get that stubbornness from?

74
00:04:47,467 --> 00:04:49,134
That little thing, honestly.

75
00:05:00,353 --> 00:05:01,980
Who's there?

76
00:05:04,807 --> 00:05:07,054
What are you doing sitting in the dark?

77
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:08,445
I thought you were a ghost.

78
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:13,518
When you left earlier you looked like
a man heading out on a first date,

79
00:05:13,526 --> 00:05:15,600
thrilled with the whole world,

80
00:05:16,421 --> 00:05:18,762
so what did you say to the boy?

81
00:05:19,282 --> 00:05:21,980
Did you go with "I am your father?"

82
00:05:25,921 --> 00:05:26,953
Right.

83
00:05:27,053 --> 00:05:31,394
You wouldn't ask a child
something like that.

84
00:05:31,989 --> 00:05:33,761
I asked Gyu Rim,

85
00:05:36,387 --> 00:05:38,887
- and she says he isn't mine.
- And?

86
00:05:38,994 --> 00:05:41,021
So he's that monkey-faced man's son?

87
00:05:41,046 --> 00:05:42,599
She was two-timing you?

88
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:45,220
Gyu Rim says she wasn't,

89
00:05:46,728 --> 00:05:48,821
but I don't think that's the truth.

90
00:05:49,274 --> 00:05:51,711
Right, I don't think it adds up either...

91
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:57,623
No, I can't lose my head over this too.

92
00:05:58,094 --> 00:06:01,900
But his burger order is exactly the same.

93
00:06:02,234 --> 00:06:04,034
No onions or pickles, add a fried egg.

94
00:06:04,059 --> 00:06:06,504
No onions or pickles, add a fried egg.

95
00:06:07,043 --> 00:06:08,076
That's my order too.

96
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:09,827
So does that make me your son as well?

97
00:06:11,377 --> 00:06:12,414
Fair point.

98
00:06:14,221 --> 00:06:16,147
What is wrong with me?

99
00:06:17,161 --> 00:06:20,807
When someone says no,
I should take it as a no and give up,

100
00:06:23,213 --> 00:06:26,020
but why am I still hung up
on a married woman?

101
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:29,873
Am I out of my mind?

102
00:06:30,513 --> 00:06:32,327
Of course you are. Completely.

103
00:06:32,523 --> 00:06:36,670
Seo Hyeon, Yun Jin,
nobody thinks you're sane.

104
00:06:36,834 --> 00:06:40,254
Lose it any further
and I'll commit you myself!

105
00:06:59,069 --> 00:07:01,314
Get up. Get up right now.

106
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,420
Where do you think you are,
lying around like this?

107
00:07:04,614 --> 00:07:05,974
What are you on about?

108
00:07:06,001 --> 00:07:08,754
I went to bed at dawn.
Don't wake me up. It's Sunday.

109
00:07:08,801 --> 00:07:11,000
Go sleep at your own place.

110
00:07:11,094 --> 00:07:12,927
Get out of my house right now.

111
00:07:14,594 --> 00:07:16,874
What nonsense is this so early?

112
00:07:16,921 --> 00:07:19,507
I'm telling you to move out
of my house, right now.

113
00:07:19,527 --> 00:07:20,541
Han Gyu Rim.

114
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:22,014
Do I know you?

115
00:07:22,181 --> 00:07:24,121
What's this act now?

116
00:07:27,401 --> 00:07:28,521
What is it?

117
00:07:28,547 --> 00:07:30,382
I've packed all your things,

118
00:07:30,571 --> 00:07:32,714
so just get up and walk out.

119
00:07:32,894 --> 00:07:34,534
The door is this way.

120
00:07:34,559 --> 00:07:37,007
- Are you insane?
- You're the insane one.

121
00:07:37,087 --> 00:07:39,767
Sleeping in this late in someone's house.

122
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,014
Will you leave quietly,
or after I hit you?

123
00:07:47,067 --> 00:07:48,607
Is this about yesterday's family meeting?

124
00:07:48,747 --> 00:07:50,119
Are you sulking because I said
you and Dad couldn't come?

125
00:07:50,121 --> 00:07:51,521
Is that why you're being childish?

126
00:07:51,627 --> 00:07:53,393
Dad? Since when is he your dad?

127
00:07:53,907 --> 00:07:55,385
You have a separate father.

128
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,627
"Dad."

129
00:07:56,861 --> 00:07:59,021
You were absolutely dripping with charm.

130
00:07:59,127 --> 00:08:00,821
What are you talking about?

131
00:08:03,574 --> 00:08:04,600
You saw me?

132
00:08:04,627 --> 00:08:05,803
Get out. Now.

133
00:08:06,017 --> 00:08:08,072
I don't have a sister like you,

134
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,861
and Dad doesn't have a daughter
like you either. Get out.

135
00:08:10,916 --> 00:08:12,758
I'm asking if you came
to the family meeting.

136
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,214
How much did you see?

137
00:08:15,686 --> 00:08:17,966
However ashamed you are of us,
this is too far.

138
00:08:18,139 --> 00:08:20,725
Who hires an actor to get married?

139
00:08:21,007 --> 00:08:22,791
You studied medicine and went abroad,

140
00:08:22,812 --> 00:08:25,748
just to end up pulling a con like this?

141
00:08:27,207 --> 00:08:29,355
Before I go to your in-laws
and tell them everything,

142
00:08:29,409 --> 00:08:31,314
be honest with them and ask forgiveness.

143
00:08:31,474 --> 00:08:33,456
If our family embarrasses you that much,

144
00:08:33,683 --> 00:08:36,897
say you're cutting ties with us,

145
00:08:37,032 --> 00:08:38,880
and none of us will show our faces
before you until the day we die.

146
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,973
What do you mean?

147
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,494
I went to that family meeting.

148
00:09:08,519 --> 00:09:10,059
Even though you told me not to.

149
00:09:12,734 --> 00:09:13,947
You did the right thing.

150
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:18,514
That's it? That's all you're going to say?

151
00:09:21,057 --> 00:09:26,121
Knowing you, you must have agonized
over it before you went.

152
00:09:26,389 --> 00:09:30,525
You didn't want to, but you had no choice.

153
00:09:31,105 --> 00:09:32,373
It must have been hard on you.

154
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,116
Should I say more?

155
00:09:37,446 --> 00:09:38,569
The thing is,

156
00:09:39,837 --> 00:09:41,653
it was Gyu Yeong's family meeting.

157
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:43,813
That girl's name is Gyu Yeong...

158
00:09:48,228 --> 00:09:49,241
Who?

159
00:09:50,227 --> 00:09:51,331
That's right.

160
00:09:52,085 --> 00:09:55,567
Not someone with the same name,
and I'm not confused or mistaken.

161
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:58,988
The one who came to mind
the moment you heard the name.

162
00:09:59,936 --> 00:10:01,834
Your daughter, Han Gyu Yeong.

163
00:10:04,153 --> 00:10:08,614
Why did you go to her family meeting?

164
00:10:09,913 --> 00:10:11,746
And what was her father doing?

165
00:10:16,599 --> 00:10:19,359
What was her father doing
that you had to go?

166
00:10:19,734 --> 00:10:23,001
I'm not sure.
It seemed she had her reasons.

167
00:10:25,386 --> 00:10:27,359
Did Gyu Yeong ask you to?

168
00:10:34,327 --> 00:10:36,253
What on earth was she thinking...

169
00:10:38,647 --> 00:10:41,180
How did you meet Gyu Yeong?

170
00:10:43,093 --> 00:10:44,407
Honestly,

171
00:10:46,014 --> 00:10:48,847
she came to find me nine years ago,

172
00:10:49,814 --> 00:10:50,887
after she learned we'd remarried.

173
00:10:55,274 --> 00:10:57,776
Why didn't you tell me back then?

174
00:10:57,801 --> 00:11:01,374
Because Gyu Yeong begged me
never to tell you.

175
00:11:03,461 --> 00:11:06,487
And after that, she called
for the first time in years.

176
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:09,330
I never meant to deceive you.

177
00:11:10,082 --> 00:11:13,341
I was going to tell you openly
when the time was right.

178
00:11:14,087 --> 00:11:17,206
Anyway, after going
to the family meeting like this,

179
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:20,800
I felt I couldn't put it off any longer,
so I'm telling you now.

180
00:11:21,486 --> 00:11:25,753
Honey, I'm sorry
I couldn't tell you sooner.

181
00:11:32,407 --> 00:11:36,320
Honey.

182
00:11:41,274 --> 00:11:44,499
Why are you apologizing?

183
00:11:44,993 --> 00:11:47,066
I'm the one who should be sorry,

184
00:11:47,427 --> 00:11:49,753
and you're only making it worse.

185
00:11:57,234 --> 00:12:01,475
I'm truly sorry for putting you
in such a difficult position.

186
00:12:02,834 --> 00:12:05,181
Why would you say that?

187
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:10,154
Honey, your child is my child too.

188
00:12:10,179 --> 00:12:12,732
That's why I went to that meeting.

189
00:12:13,024 --> 00:12:15,136
I'm a father too, aren't I?

190
00:12:15,512 --> 00:12:17,479
It's all right. Don't talk like that.

191
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:21,313
The meeting went well, so it's all right.

192
00:12:35,047 --> 00:12:38,020
Han Gyu Rim, if you breathe a word
of this to my in-laws,

193
00:12:38,273 --> 00:12:40,886
neither of us walks away from it.

194
00:12:47,121 --> 00:12:49,020
I wouldn't be like this
if I had any choice.

195
00:12:49,114 --> 00:12:51,387
All they ever did was make my life harder,
just because we're family.

196
00:12:51,474 --> 00:12:53,287
What have they ever done for me, anyway?

197
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:56,320
When I was struggling,
did they ever give me a dime?

198
00:13:07,656 --> 00:13:10,416
(Wedding gift and Household Essentials)

199
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,974
What am I going to do about the gifts?

200
00:13:18,161 --> 00:13:19,781
Han Gyu O.

201
00:13:21,486 --> 00:13:22,794
Where did he go?

202
00:13:50,346 --> 00:13:52,733
This is better than most boutiques.

203
00:14:12,213 --> 00:14:13,233
What are you doing?

204
00:14:15,661 --> 00:14:17,301
Well, what would I be doing?

205
00:14:17,534 --> 00:14:19,807
There's just a lot of nice things,
so I was having a look.

206
00:14:19,874 --> 00:14:21,916
These days the oversized
and boyfriend looks,

207
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,414
are so pretty.

208
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:28,718
You, who always wears things so tight
your blood barely circulates?

209
00:14:29,105 --> 00:14:30,180
All of a sudden?

210
00:14:30,886 --> 00:14:32,653
If you wanted the boyfriend look,

211
00:14:32,678 --> 00:14:34,853
wear your boyfriend's clothes.
Why dig through my closet?

212
00:14:35,001 --> 00:14:36,473
Who's digging?

213
00:14:36,606 --> 00:14:38,159
I told you I was just looking.

214
00:14:39,347 --> 00:14:41,707
You look with your arms
instead of your eyes?

215
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:46,207
For someone just looking,
it's quite something.

216
00:14:46,227 --> 00:14:48,107
You picked out only the expensive ones.

217
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:52,034
They wouldn't fit your boyfriend.

218
00:14:54,686 --> 00:14:57,621
What, were you going to sell them
behind my back?

219
00:14:59,753 --> 00:15:00,973
For goodness' sake!

220
00:15:01,327 --> 00:15:02,441
I'm so sick of this.

221
00:15:02,474 --> 00:15:04,714
What? Do you need money?

222
00:15:05,627 --> 00:15:07,994
How badly do you need money
to go through my closet?

223
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,240
Do you have any money?

224
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:12,532
How much could you lend me...

225
00:15:12,607 --> 00:15:15,333
I mean, could you gather up
every cent you have and lend it to me?

226
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,071
You know my in-laws are seriously rich.

227
00:15:18,293 --> 00:15:20,114
A year? No, six months?

228
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,326
No, I could pay it all back
within three months.

229
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,615
Gyu O, you're doing well, aren't you?

230
00:15:24,774 --> 00:15:26,849
If you say you're struggling
or that you need something,

231
00:15:26,877 --> 00:15:28,734
there are plenty of women
who'd hand it right over.

232
00:15:28,759 --> 00:15:31,614
You can make thousands,
even millions, whenever you want.

233
00:15:32,673 --> 00:15:35,474
I'm not asking you to give it to me.
I'm asking you to lend it.

234
00:15:35,878 --> 00:15:37,431
I'll pay double the bank interest.

235
00:15:39,781 --> 00:15:41,445
You,

236
00:15:41,936 --> 00:15:46,814
you know exactly how I earn that money,
and it doesn't bother you?

237
00:15:47,221 --> 00:15:48,921
You can spend it with a clear conscience?

238
00:15:49,594 --> 00:15:50,594
Well?

239
00:15:51,588 --> 00:15:53,904
Someone else told me it was filthy money,

240
00:15:54,018 --> 00:15:56,420
and threw a fit saying
he couldn't take it.

241
00:15:57,294 --> 00:15:58,754
What are you talking about so suddenly?

242
00:15:59,769 --> 00:16:02,521
Nothing. It just made me feel
like he was really family.

243
00:16:05,094 --> 00:16:07,101
So what am I, fake family?

244
00:16:07,304 --> 00:16:09,320
I'm the one who stays cool
about what you do,

245
00:16:09,381 --> 00:16:11,114
and accepts it without judgment.

246
00:16:11,116 --> 00:16:13,010
- Get out.
- Gyu O!

247
00:16:13,035 --> 00:16:15,864
I suddenly don't want
to talk to you. Get out.

248
00:16:15,889 --> 00:16:18,235
- Han Gyu O.
- Even if money rotted in my hands,

249
00:16:19,062 --> 00:16:21,706
I wouldn't give you a single cent,
so get out. Now.

250
00:16:21,731 --> 00:16:23,194
- Hey.
- Get lost.

251
00:16:32,321 --> 00:16:34,287
Who told him
he had to make money that way?

252
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:35,973
He chose to live like that.

253
00:16:38,507 --> 00:16:40,793
If he didn't want to lend it,
he could've just said so,

254
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,945
instead of making me feel
like some kind of jerk.

255
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:48,727
Whatever.

256
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:05,847
Get it together, Han Gyu Rim.

257
00:17:05,872 --> 00:17:08,653
You don't look well at all.

258
00:17:09,526 --> 00:17:11,560
Never mind that. You stay here.

259
00:17:11,654 --> 00:17:13,907
I'll run over there instead.

260
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,416
No, I'm fine.

261
00:17:15,558 --> 00:17:16,614
Everything's fine now.

262
00:17:16,639 --> 00:17:17,845
Are you sure?

263
00:17:20,194 --> 00:17:21,620
I'm off on the delivery.

264
00:17:21,687 --> 00:17:24,181
When times are hard,
even smiling takes effort.

265
00:17:24,247 --> 00:17:26,407
Don't force yourself to smile.

266
00:17:27,992 --> 00:17:30,299
Is something troubling her again?

267
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:34,400
Has some woman wrung her out again?

268
00:17:36,681 --> 00:17:38,243
Su Nam.

269
00:17:39,047 --> 00:17:41,160
Your mom just left.

270
00:17:41,834 --> 00:17:43,321
Hey, you're a tiny thing,

271
00:17:43,346 --> 00:17:45,425
so why are you clutching your back?

272
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:47,714
I twisted it picking up a ball earlier.

273
00:17:48,507 --> 00:17:50,163
I'm not here for my mom.

274
00:17:50,188 --> 00:17:51,851
Where is Cho Heung Sik?

275
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,113
Heung Sik? He's right over there.

276
00:17:56,934 --> 00:17:58,861
- Heung Sik.
- Gyeol.

277
00:17:59,208 --> 00:18:03,464
Didn't you say your back
was acting up today too?

278
00:18:03,984 --> 00:18:05,019
Good timing.

279
00:18:05,394 --> 00:18:07,814
The two of you have somewhere
to go together.

280
00:18:08,373 --> 00:18:10,920
If you have business with him,
take care of it there.

281
00:18:13,067 --> 00:18:14,742
Shall we? Let's go.

282
00:18:14,767 --> 00:18:16,720
- Take care.
- My back.

283
00:18:23,906 --> 00:18:25,039
Heung Sik.

284
00:18:25,921 --> 00:18:27,494
Yes? What is it?

285
00:18:27,519 --> 00:18:29,959
Answer my question honestly.

286
00:18:30,501 --> 00:18:31,704
In all my eight years of life,

287
00:18:31,729 --> 00:18:33,858
this is truly important.

288
00:18:34,287 --> 00:18:35,934
And look at my face while you answer.

289
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:40,793
All right, ask away.

290
00:18:40,818 --> 00:18:45,002
The man from the game
we met at the police station,

291
00:18:45,229 --> 00:18:47,240
you'd met him before, hadn't you?

292
00:18:48,149 --> 00:18:51,500
No. That was the first time.

293
00:18:52,686 --> 00:18:54,820
Then why were you so flustered?

294
00:18:55,497 --> 00:18:58,799
I wasn't. Nothing like that happened.
You saw it wrong.

295
00:18:58,861 --> 00:19:00,934
I said look at my face.

296
00:19:04,123 --> 00:19:07,901
And why has my mom been so strange?

297
00:19:08,787 --> 00:19:10,207
What's strange about her?

298
00:19:10,334 --> 00:19:11,919
She seemed perfectly normal to me.

299
00:19:12,027 --> 00:19:13,272
She isn't.

300
00:19:13,686 --> 00:19:16,007
Ever since she met the man from the game,

301
00:19:16,367 --> 00:19:18,827
my mom has been very strange.

302
00:19:20,001 --> 00:19:21,217
No, she hasn't.

303
00:19:21,242 --> 00:19:25,642
I saw her briefly this morning
and she was completely normal.

304
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:34,247
My mom says she doesn't like him.

305
00:19:35,221 --> 00:19:37,220
Well, who'd like someone
they met at a police station?

306
00:19:37,245 --> 00:19:38,872
She says she doesn't like him
because she doesn't.

307
00:19:38,897 --> 00:19:40,027
What does that mean?

308
00:19:40,144 --> 00:19:41,693
How can you dislike someone
because you dislike them?

309
00:19:41,718 --> 00:19:44,377
A negative plus a negative
makes a strong positive.

310
00:19:44,593 --> 00:19:46,819
It means she likes him. A lot.

311
00:19:48,316 --> 00:19:49,627
That can't be right.

312
00:19:49,652 --> 00:19:52,665
Your mom said she'd
completely forgotten him.

313
00:19:53,121 --> 00:19:55,793
Sure, back then they were mad
about each other,

314
00:19:55,818 --> 00:19:57,991
but that was already eight years ago.

315
00:20:02,606 --> 00:20:03,674
Gyeol,

316
00:20:05,335 --> 00:20:07,554
I've got something urgent,

317
00:20:08,315 --> 00:20:10,953
so if you've said everything, may I go?

318
00:20:14,526 --> 00:20:15,869
(Jameon Medical Supplies)

319
00:20:15,894 --> 00:20:19,180
- Good work, Lee Guk.
- Yes, Heung Sik.

320
00:21:09,994 --> 00:21:11,520
Hey.

321
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,585
- Why are you throwing this out?
- It tastes awful.

322
00:21:15,934 --> 00:21:17,334
Hold on.

323
00:21:23,387 --> 00:21:25,927
What's so awful about it? It's delicious.

324
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:33,507
It's actually the best thing
you've cooked lately.

325
00:21:33,547 --> 00:21:36,567
- Don't overdo it. Hand it over.
- I'm not overdoing it. I mean it.

326
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,907
I think your taste buds are broken.

327
00:21:44,201 --> 00:21:46,120
Now that I try it again,
it's not that good.

328
00:21:46,174 --> 00:21:47,940
- Give it here.
- Actually, it's not bad at all.

329
00:21:47,954 --> 00:21:49,321
Don't mess with me.

330
00:21:49,346 --> 00:21:51,496
I'm telling you, it's really good.

331
00:21:51,701 --> 00:21:53,141
Just let the staff taste it too.

332
00:21:53,166 --> 00:21:54,432
Hand it over while I'm asking nicely.

333
00:21:54,593 --> 00:21:56,780
That doesn't sound very nice to me.

334
00:22:05,259 --> 00:22:07,793
- You ordered side dishes and kimchi?
- Yes.

335
00:22:08,368 --> 00:22:09,728
- Yes.
- Take that, would you?

336
00:22:10,686 --> 00:22:12,372
- Hurry and set up.
- Yes.

337
00:22:22,807 --> 00:22:24,693
This is really good.

338
00:22:25,550 --> 00:22:27,523
- It's incredible.
- Truly?

339
00:22:29,178 --> 00:22:30,847
I just saw my mom in that.

340
00:22:30,861 --> 00:22:32,461
With this alone
I could eat two bowls of rice.

341
00:22:32,462 --> 00:22:34,578
You eat two bowls with nothing at all.

342
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:35,926
How did you know?

343
00:22:36,147 --> 00:22:37,320
The chef isn't eating?

344
00:22:38,413 --> 00:22:40,346
This is amazing.

345
00:22:42,179 --> 00:22:43,192
There we go!

346
00:22:46,417 --> 00:22:48,524
- Here you are.
- You must be a wonderful cook.

347
00:22:48,657 --> 00:22:50,436
Our staff are terribly picky eaters.

348
00:22:50,675 --> 00:22:51,911
Thank you.

349
00:22:52,245 --> 00:22:53,487
Please order often.

350
00:22:53,541 --> 00:22:56,388
Anything over 50 dollars
ships free of charge,

351
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:59,840
If you order from us often, I'll throw
in extras and let you try our new dishes.

352
00:22:59,865 --> 00:23:00,877
Understood.

353
00:23:01,335 --> 00:23:02,341
Enjoy your meal.

354
00:23:02,366 --> 00:23:04,112
- Thank you.
- Thank you. It's really good.

355
00:23:04,137 --> 00:23:05,286
It's absolutely delicious.

356
00:23:05,788 --> 00:23:07,488
Where's the restroom?

357
00:23:07,981 --> 00:23:09,668
Go that way and turn right.

358
00:23:09,761 --> 00:23:11,550
- Thank you.
- Yes, take care.

359
00:23:11,638 --> 00:23:13,581
- I'm starving.
- Help yourselves.

360
00:23:16,681 --> 00:23:19,201
- After making it this good...
- Why are you taking that out?

361
00:23:19,202 --> 00:23:20,609
Watch how you talk to me.

362
00:23:21,248 --> 00:23:22,845
You're making me want to swear.

363
00:23:27,994 --> 00:23:31,181
Mom's Side Dishes closed suddenly,
so we ordered from somewhere else,

364
00:23:31,401 --> 00:23:32,801
and it's apparently a huge hit.

365
00:23:33,475 --> 00:23:34,799
There's a huge hit right here too.

366
00:23:34,801 --> 00:23:37,294
- Try this as well.
- What is it? A new dish?

367
00:23:37,295 --> 00:23:38,389
It looks really good.

368
00:23:38,521 --> 00:23:40,501
It's terrible. Don't eat it.

369
00:23:41,631 --> 00:23:42,651
Try this.

370
00:23:46,428 --> 00:23:47,986
Where is this from?

371
00:23:48,014 --> 00:23:50,044
What is this? It's incredible.

372
00:23:50,046 --> 00:23:51,446
- It's really good.
- Isn't it?

373
00:23:51,448 --> 00:23:52,455
Really good? My foot.

374
00:23:53,449 --> 00:23:54,994
See? I told you it was a hit.

375
00:23:59,088 --> 00:24:01,867
This one's a hit too.

376
00:24:01,935 --> 00:24:03,515
Right? It's the real thing.

377
00:24:03,608 --> 00:24:05,501
- Mom's Side Dishes can't even compete.
- Right.

378
00:24:05,608 --> 00:24:07,848
Mu Jin, you try this too.

379
00:24:07,850 --> 00:24:09,796
It's far better than my mom's cooking.
Can you believe it?

380
00:24:09,870 --> 00:24:11,594
I'm not eating it.
You touched it with your bare hands.

381
00:24:12,027 --> 00:24:14,887
Don't eat it, then. It's your loss.

382
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:18,054
What is this? It's no joke.

383
00:24:20,401 --> 00:24:22,293
- Sit down and eat.
- Yes.

384
00:24:23,659 --> 00:24:24,672
What now?

385
00:24:29,821 --> 00:24:31,115
This is Han Gyeol.

386
00:24:31,396 --> 00:24:34,354
If you're not busy,
could we meet for a moment?

387
00:24:36,581 --> 00:24:39,822
We can. Absolutely.

388
00:24:44,808 --> 00:24:46,325
What's got into him now?

389
00:24:46,355 --> 00:24:47,554
He's impossible to keep up with.

390
00:24:50,441 --> 00:24:53,343
I'm heading out for a moment,
so enjoy your meal,

391
00:24:53,607 --> 00:24:57,607
and let's consider putting this dish
on the regular menu.

392
00:24:57,661 --> 00:24:59,607
Come to think of it, the taste wasn't bad.

393
00:25:00,767 --> 00:25:02,447
- Yes, Chef.
- Enjoy your meal!

394
00:25:03,294 --> 00:25:04,746
- Off you go.
- Take care.

395
00:25:09,101 --> 00:25:13,674
People who never had a proper adolescence
sometimes hit their midlife slump early.

396
00:25:13,834 --> 00:25:15,379
"Our chef has lost his mind."

397
00:25:15,381 --> 00:25:16,525
Instead of cursing him inwardly,

398
00:25:16,719 --> 00:25:18,395
"What a shame at such a young age."

399
00:25:18,420 --> 00:25:19,768
Let's take pity on him instead.

400
00:25:19,988 --> 00:25:21,034
- Everyone, eat up.
- Yes.

401
00:25:21,388 --> 00:25:23,281
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yes.

402
00:25:25,655 --> 00:25:28,221
But where is this place, really?

403
00:25:28,541 --> 00:25:31,387
You want to relabel it
and sell it as our own menu, right?

404
00:25:31,402 --> 00:25:32,421
Exactly.

405
00:26:05,376 --> 00:26:08,508
This is Gyu Yeong's business card.

406
00:26:13,388 --> 00:26:15,681
Give her a call.

407
00:26:16,401 --> 00:26:20,141
With the wedding coming up,
she must feel so lost and anxious.

408
00:26:21,035 --> 00:26:23,735
You said her sister is only a year older.

409
00:26:25,394 --> 00:26:27,253
There must be so much
you could help her with...

410
00:26:28,582 --> 00:26:31,295
(Cliad Medical Skin Clinic)

411
00:26:49,188 --> 00:26:51,004
I'm telling you, it's authentic.

412
00:26:51,398 --> 00:26:54,681
You checked the certificate,
the authentication, and the receipt.

413
00:26:55,021 --> 00:26:58,097
You clearly said you'd only
carried it three or four times,

414
00:26:58,392 --> 00:27:01,208
but looking closely,
there seem to be a lot of scratches.

415
00:27:01,708 --> 00:27:03,858
I saw the exact same one online,

416
00:27:03,926 --> 00:27:07,635
and with scratches like these,
it was about 1,000 dollars cheaper.

417
00:27:09,035 --> 00:27:12,601
Then go buy that one
that's 1,000 dollars cheaper.

418
00:27:12,987 --> 00:27:14,000
No.

419
00:27:15,695 --> 00:27:17,921
I really do love it,

420
00:27:17,946 --> 00:27:19,738
so could you take off another 700 dollars?

421
00:27:19,970 --> 00:27:22,807
Or at least 500 dollars?

422
00:27:22,981 --> 00:27:26,254
I saw plenty of other bags
and shoes on your seller page,

423
00:27:26,667 --> 00:27:28,763
and I'll buy more of them later.

424
00:27:29,135 --> 00:27:30,711
I'll recommend you to my friends too.

425
00:27:30,713 --> 00:27:32,728
Recommend, my foot.

426
00:27:33,548 --> 00:27:36,116
What did you just say?

427
00:27:36,249 --> 00:27:37,254
Why?

428
00:27:37,475 --> 00:27:39,652
So you can wear them down too,

429
00:27:39,693 --> 00:27:42,190
nitpick and haggle them into the ground
and take them for nothing?

430
00:27:42,584 --> 00:27:45,032
Forget it. I'm not selling to you.

431
00:27:47,835 --> 00:27:49,310
Unbelievable.

432
00:27:50,084 --> 00:27:51,515
You're just a bag seller,
for crying out loud.

433
00:27:56,561 --> 00:27:58,294
Say I came out here to sell a bag.

434
00:27:58,615 --> 00:28:00,354
What did you come out to sell,
your conscience?

435
00:28:01,501 --> 00:28:06,058
Circumstances forced me to knock
1,000 dollars off this pristine bag,

436
00:28:06,659 --> 00:28:08,905
and you want another 1,000 off that?

437
00:28:10,341 --> 00:28:13,289
I'd rather not sell it.
I'm not that desperate.

438
00:28:14,975 --> 00:28:17,970
You're so young, but you already go crazy
over designer goods!

439
00:28:17,972 --> 00:28:18,974
Hey!

440
00:28:21,935 --> 00:28:23,195
What did you just say?

441
00:28:26,675 --> 00:28:29,583
All that designer gear from head to toe,

442
00:28:30,211 --> 00:28:31,882
you didn't buy any of it
with your own money, did you?

443
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:33,805
Did your parents buy it?

444
00:28:34,086 --> 00:28:35,281
Did some man buy it for you?

445
00:28:36,181 --> 00:28:37,535
Barely out of your teens.

446
00:28:38,068 --> 00:28:39,733
Stick to canvas bags.

447
00:28:39,735 --> 00:28:41,794
That's about your level, sweetheart.

448
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,113
Pathetic, honestly.

449
00:28:46,995 --> 00:28:49,288
Out here selling bags
because you're broke.

450
00:28:49,715 --> 00:28:52,659
You'd better take a hard look
at your own level,

451
00:28:52,661 --> 00:28:54,388
if you don't want to end up
begging in your old age!

452
00:29:01,134 --> 00:29:02,268
My precious.

453
00:29:21,028 --> 00:29:22,288
Han Gyu Yeong, of all people.

454
00:29:23,696 --> 00:29:26,288
How did I end up in this state?

455
00:29:41,340 --> 00:29:43,661
Somebody give me a reason today.

456
00:29:45,715 --> 00:29:46,741
Hello?

457
00:29:49,175 --> 00:29:51,578
Hello?

458
00:29:54,035 --> 00:29:57,384
Who is this? If you're going to call,
you should say something.

459
00:29:58,510 --> 00:30:00,588
What? Is this a prank call?

460
00:30:00,721 --> 00:30:02,028
Do you want to die today?

461
00:30:02,048 --> 00:30:03,928
Where are you? What's your name?

462
00:30:04,621 --> 00:30:06,501
Is this Han Gyu Yeong's phone?

463
00:30:09,221 --> 00:30:11,114
It is. Who's calling?

464
00:30:11,489 --> 00:30:15,181
Gyu Yeong. It's Mom.

465
00:30:27,234 --> 00:30:28,399
You're here?

466
00:30:52,821 --> 00:30:55,198
- You're Gyu Yeong, right?
- Yes.

467
00:30:56,768 --> 00:30:58,170
It's been a long time, Mom.

468
00:31:01,067 --> 00:31:02,801
- Sit down.
- Yes.

469
00:31:11,901 --> 00:31:13,780
You've grown even more beautiful.

470
00:31:14,668 --> 00:31:15,788
And more elegant.

471
00:31:18,275 --> 00:31:20,503
I think I used to speak casually to you,

472
00:31:20,978 --> 00:31:22,695
but it doesn't feel right anymore...

473
00:31:23,057 --> 00:31:24,868
I became a doctor.

474
00:31:25,195 --> 00:31:27,314
I studied so hard,

475
00:31:27,642 --> 00:31:29,688
so I could tell you proudly
when I saw you.

476
00:31:31,595 --> 00:31:32,908
I missed you, Mom.

477
00:31:37,215 --> 00:31:38,222
Why did you do it?

478
00:31:39,542 --> 00:31:40,553
Sorry?

479
00:31:43,075 --> 00:31:44,848
Here's your tangerine tea.

480
00:31:47,115 --> 00:31:48,448
What would you like?

481
00:31:50,721 --> 00:31:52,802
I'll order in a moment.

482
00:31:53,630 --> 00:31:54,634
Yes.

483
00:32:08,668 --> 00:32:10,448
Why did you go to my husband?

484
00:32:12,048 --> 00:32:15,354
If you had something to say,
you should have come to me first.

485
00:32:16,448 --> 00:32:18,033
Why did you go to him?

486
00:32:18,035 --> 00:32:21,008
And told him to keep it from me.

487
00:32:24,309 --> 00:32:26,313
I'm sorry. It's just,

488
00:32:27,401 --> 00:32:29,416
you'd remarried and were living well,

489
00:32:29,816 --> 00:32:32,200
and I thought turning up suddenly
would make you uncomfortable.

490
00:32:32,202 --> 00:32:33,840
You knew it would be uncomfortable,

491
00:32:34,701 --> 00:32:37,568
but it never occurred to you how
difficult a position I'd be in?

492
00:32:39,795 --> 00:32:42,295
A doctor without that much sense?

493
00:32:44,741 --> 00:32:45,763
I'm sorry.

494
00:32:46,471 --> 00:32:48,001
Is sorry enough?

495
00:32:50,354 --> 00:32:52,573
I heard you even asked him
to attend the family meeting.

496
00:32:54,207 --> 00:32:56,599
And what was your father doing?

497
00:32:57,678 --> 00:32:59,588
Is he dead?

498
00:33:02,616 --> 00:33:06,381
If my father came,
he'd ruin the whole marriage.

499
00:33:07,241 --> 00:33:09,411
You know exactly what kind of man he is.

500
00:33:10,004 --> 00:33:13,301
My in-laws are a wonderful family.

501
00:33:14,681 --> 00:33:17,876
This is the first stroke of luck
in my life. Do you know how far I've come?

502
00:33:18,461 --> 00:33:20,457
It's a marriage I have to make happen,

503
00:33:20,605 --> 00:33:22,961
so I knew it was rude,
but I had to ask him.

504
00:33:23,141 --> 00:33:24,831
You really think,

505
00:33:25,748 --> 00:33:26,886
that's something to say?

506
00:33:29,535 --> 00:33:32,568
How on earth did your father raise you?

507
00:33:32,981 --> 00:33:34,506
Father didn't raise us.

508
00:33:34,508 --> 00:33:35,775
We raised ourselves.

509
00:33:36,437 --> 00:33:40,281
And you ran off
and left us when we were small.

510
00:33:41,761 --> 00:33:43,454
I never ran off.

511
00:33:44,987 --> 00:33:47,961
I was thrown out by your father,
who'd found another woman.

512
00:33:49,207 --> 00:33:51,146
I couldn't take Gyu Rim,
being the eldest daughter,

513
00:33:51,768 --> 00:33:53,397
and I couldn't take Gyu O, being a son.

514
00:33:54,894 --> 00:33:57,600
I tried to take you at least,
but you said this.

515
00:33:58,648 --> 00:34:01,101
That you didn't want to go
with a poor mother.

516
00:34:01,868 --> 00:34:03,721
That you'd stay with your rich father.

517
00:34:14,228 --> 00:34:15,606
That's 10,000 dollars.

518
00:34:17,414 --> 00:34:19,255
You must need a lot. Put it toward that.

519
00:34:21,914 --> 00:34:23,161
That's all?

520
00:34:25,001 --> 00:34:26,937
You hand me 10,000 dollars
and that's the end of it?

521
00:34:27,038 --> 00:34:28,066
Gyu Yeong.

522
00:34:28,091 --> 00:34:29,855
I'm the daughter you haven't seen
in 17 years.

523
00:34:31,274 --> 00:34:33,120
What kind of mother acts like this?

524
00:34:36,215 --> 00:34:38,194
I thought you'd cry the moment you saw me,

525
00:34:38,442 --> 00:34:40,421
or at least hold me once.

526
00:34:41,648 --> 00:34:43,507
I thought you'd ask
what sort of man I'm marrying,

527
00:34:43,848 --> 00:34:46,814
or whether anything was hard for me!

528
00:34:54,140 --> 00:34:59,185
I hear you asked my husband
to come to the wedding as well.

529
00:35:01,013 --> 00:35:02,295
That can't happen.

530
00:35:02,614 --> 00:35:04,895
- I won't let him go.
- Mom!

531
00:35:04,897 --> 00:35:07,441
Just because you've lost your mind
doesn't mean the rest of us can.

532
00:35:09,341 --> 00:35:10,701
Then should I call the whole thing off?

533
00:35:10,874 --> 00:35:12,354
After the family meeting and everything?

534
00:35:12,854 --> 00:35:15,059
You take responsibility
for what you started.

535
00:35:17,120 --> 00:35:18,588
You're an adult.

536
00:35:22,207 --> 00:35:25,981
Were you always this cold and frightening?

537
00:35:31,905 --> 00:35:36,674
How do you think I got here?

538
00:35:40,068 --> 00:35:43,868
I was thrown out with nothing
and hit the very bottom of this world.

539
00:35:46,220 --> 00:35:48,323
How do you think I made it this far?

540
00:35:51,973 --> 00:35:58,359
Right now my family
matters more to me than my own life.

541
00:36:00,182 --> 00:36:02,196
I never want to lose family again.

542
00:36:05,414 --> 00:36:07,014
So help me out here.

543
00:36:09,108 --> 00:36:11,421
Never contact my husband again.

544
00:36:19,054 --> 00:36:20,199
I'm asking you.

545
00:37:40,741 --> 00:37:42,555
- Hello?
- Hey there, gigolo.

546
00:37:42,627 --> 00:37:45,047
You really want free meals
from the state that badly?

547
00:37:56,688 --> 00:38:00,101
- The number you have dialed...
- This bird, honestly!

548
00:38:02,421 --> 00:38:05,541
Fine. This isn't the only
payphone in the world,

549
00:38:06,247 --> 00:38:08,876
so let's see which of us wins.

550
00:38:09,641 --> 00:38:12,398
I won't give up until
I've snapped that bird's legs.

551
00:38:18,088 --> 00:38:19,553
I think it's around here somewhere...

552
00:38:23,014 --> 00:38:25,121
Side dish delivery.

553
00:38:28,728 --> 00:38:29,764
Come on in.

554
00:38:30,851 --> 00:38:32,394
Su Nam.

555
00:38:32,894 --> 00:38:34,347
Now who might this be?

556
00:38:34,695 --> 00:38:37,068
I definitely know this face.

557
00:38:37,508 --> 00:38:39,261
It's me, Hui Na.

558
00:38:39,288 --> 00:38:42,031
Kwon Hui Na, Colonel Kwon Tae Su's
youngest, from Andong.

559
00:38:42,306 --> 00:38:47,139
That's right. It's Hui Na.

560
00:38:47,222 --> 00:38:49,908
- How long has it been?
- I know, Su Nam.

561
00:38:49,933 --> 00:38:52,139
I wanted to come sooner.
I'm very late, aren't I?

562
00:38:52,348 --> 00:38:54,341
It's been so long.

563
00:38:54,768 --> 00:38:58,673
Last time I saw you, you still
had a little girl in you,

564
00:38:59,274 --> 00:39:02,887
and now you've grown into a young lady.
Let me look at you.

565
00:39:04,422 --> 00:39:07,184
So, are your parents both well?

566
00:39:08,218 --> 00:39:11,608
And your brother Hui Seop, he's well too?

567
00:39:11,684 --> 00:39:14,288
Of course. When I said
I was seeing you today,

568
00:39:14,289 --> 00:39:16,195
the whole family sent their regards.

569
00:39:16,263 --> 00:39:17,294
Good.

570
00:39:18,081 --> 00:39:21,390
You must have graduated long ago,

571
00:39:22,018 --> 00:39:23,036
so what about work?

572
00:39:23,536 --> 00:39:24,540
Never mind.

573
00:39:24,741 --> 00:39:28,455
I heard people get an earful these days.

574
00:39:32,541 --> 00:39:33,552
Ta-da!

575
00:39:33,820 --> 00:39:36,234
I became a teacher, Su Nam.

576
00:39:36,395 --> 00:39:37,831
At a primary school near here.

577
00:39:37,833 --> 00:39:39,314
And I moved to this neighborhood too.

578
00:39:39,316 --> 00:39:43,721
Well done, Hui Na.

579
00:39:43,801 --> 00:39:47,141
Then since you're here,
take some side dishes with you.

580
00:39:47,143 --> 00:39:49,175
It's the meat dish you like.

581
00:39:49,177 --> 00:39:51,679
Really, it's all right, Su Nam.

582
00:39:59,661 --> 00:40:00,688
I love it.

583
00:40:04,936 --> 00:40:06,223
I'll be off, Su Nam.

584
00:40:06,225 --> 00:40:08,534
I'll come again before these run out.

585
00:40:08,536 --> 00:40:09,568
All right.

586
00:40:09,661 --> 00:40:12,401
The more you live alone,
the better you have to eat.

587
00:40:12,426 --> 00:40:14,319
Yes. I'm off. Take care.

588
00:40:14,321 --> 00:40:17,689
Watch where you're going. You'll fall.

589
00:40:20,297 --> 00:40:21,321
Sweetheart.

590
00:40:21,801 --> 00:40:23,894
You startled me!

591
00:40:24,601 --> 00:40:27,934
If you come in, at least make a sound.
You gave me a fright.

592
00:40:28,321 --> 00:40:31,000
Gyu Rim left her phone at home.

593
00:40:32,768 --> 00:40:35,048
She left her phone behind?

594
00:40:36,501 --> 00:40:38,368
Why is this phone so cold?

595
00:40:40,248 --> 00:40:43,081
It was in the freezer until just now.

596
00:40:43,981 --> 00:40:46,326
I just told Gyu Rim
it had slipped into a corner.

597
00:40:46,328 --> 00:40:47,495
That's why it was hard to find.

598
00:40:55,048 --> 00:40:57,288
Worried his sister would be embarrassed.

599
00:40:58,313 --> 00:41:01,061
He's thoughtful, that boy.

600
00:41:02,234 --> 00:41:06,420
Head to toe there isn't
one thing to throw away,

601
00:41:07,573 --> 00:41:10,066
so how did that fox tail
get in among them?

602
00:41:11,671 --> 00:41:12,894
What's it to me?

603
00:41:13,035 --> 00:41:14,508
She is not going to be my family anyway.

604
00:41:20,928 --> 00:41:22,528
What is this, a stalker?

605
00:41:34,041 --> 00:41:35,067
You know me, right?

606
00:41:35,708 --> 00:41:37,096
No, I don't.

607
00:41:38,109 --> 00:41:39,115
You really don't?

608
00:41:39,376 --> 00:41:41,793
I said I don't. Who are you?

609
00:41:41,795 --> 00:41:43,388
Then why were you so startled just now?

610
00:41:45,569 --> 00:41:46,594
What are you on about?

611
00:41:47,281 --> 00:41:50,388
I don't know how strong
your nerves happen to be,

612
00:41:50,455 --> 00:41:53,624
but when an ordinary person like me
has a stranger chasing after them,

613
00:41:54,065 --> 00:41:56,801
and staring like that,
ten out of ten would be startled.

614
00:41:58,835 --> 00:42:00,095
You really don't know me?

615
00:42:03,288 --> 00:42:05,314
Do I have to know who you are?

616
00:42:17,253 --> 00:42:21,926
I never should have gone back to him...

617
00:42:26,194 --> 00:42:27,794
Why would you go back to an ex?

618
00:42:27,796 --> 00:42:31,906
Exactly. Why did I go back to him?

619
00:42:36,148 --> 00:42:38,493
We broke up because he cheated,

620
00:42:39,401 --> 00:42:43,910
but he begged and clung to me
for a whole month.

621
00:42:44,691 --> 00:42:46,901
Saying he'd truly change,

622
00:42:47,306 --> 00:42:51,468
and asking for one more chance.

623
00:42:55,570 --> 00:42:57,101
So I,

624
00:43:01,175 --> 00:43:04,966
pretended to give in and took him back...

625
00:43:08,054 --> 00:43:10,034
A leopard doesn't change its spots.

626
00:43:21,348 --> 00:43:23,148
Drinking like that only
ruins your stomach.

627
00:43:23,268 --> 00:43:24,327
Have some broth with it.

628
00:43:34,008 --> 00:43:35,048
What's this?

629
00:43:37,245 --> 00:43:42,281
Are you worried about me right now?

630
00:43:45,268 --> 00:43:47,614
Excuse me.

631
00:43:48,429 --> 00:43:49,721
How about getting up?

632
00:43:52,454 --> 00:43:53,868
Mom,

633
00:43:54,933 --> 00:44:00,294
just five more minutes.

634
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:29,894
Don't go.

635
00:44:33,359 --> 00:44:37,058
Don't leave me alone.

636
00:44:38,739 --> 00:44:40,735
You're very drunk. Go to sleep.

637
00:44:43,794 --> 00:44:45,730
Get a grip. I'm not your boyfriend.

638
00:44:48,081 --> 00:44:49,090
I know.

639
00:44:49,721 --> 00:44:53,288
You're Han Gyu O.

640
00:46:44,393 --> 00:46:47,386
It's been a while, Han Gyu O.

641
00:46:57,901 --> 00:47:00,061
It's been a while since your last visit.

642
00:47:00,086 --> 00:47:02,504
- About two months?
- Yes.

643
00:47:02,944 --> 00:47:04,297
Have you been unwell?

644
00:47:04,543 --> 00:47:06,091
You look a little thinner.

645
00:47:06,486 --> 00:47:07,752
No, nothing's wrong...

646
00:47:07,777 --> 00:47:09,630
I just haven't had much appetite lately.

647
00:47:09,977 --> 00:47:11,913
But the noodles here go down well.

648
00:47:12,044 --> 00:47:13,677
Had I known, I'd have come days sooner.

649
00:47:13,677 --> 00:47:15,277
That's a relief.

650
00:47:15,444 --> 00:47:16,777
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yes.

651
00:47:16,777 --> 00:47:19,027
- Let me know if you need anything.
- Yes.

652
00:47:24,796 --> 00:47:25,830
Have a seat here.

653
00:47:35,457 --> 00:47:37,691
- May I share your table?
- Yes.

654
00:47:40,844 --> 00:47:42,582
- One spicy noodle soup.
- Yes.

655
00:47:54,153 --> 00:47:57,211
I happened to have the noodles here
a little while ago,

656
00:47:57,711 --> 00:47:59,611
and I couldn't stop thinking
about them, so I came back.

657
00:47:59,757 --> 00:48:00,861
I see.

658
00:48:06,926 --> 00:48:08,244
The spicy radish salad...

659
00:48:10,262 --> 00:48:12,644
Try wrapping it in the spicy radish salad.

660
00:48:12,644 --> 00:48:14,077
It's absolutely superb.

661
00:48:14,843 --> 00:48:16,050
I see.

662
00:48:19,513 --> 00:48:23,544
Trust me and try it once.

663
00:48:24,090 --> 00:48:25,190
Yes.

664
00:48:29,983 --> 00:48:33,838
Do I look like someone you can't trust?

665
00:48:35,577 --> 00:48:37,577
I only wanted you to enjoy it more,

666
00:48:38,430 --> 00:48:40,997
so I swallowed my shyness
and offered some advice.

667
00:48:41,811 --> 00:48:45,575
If only out of respect for the gesture,
please try wrapping it once.

668
00:48:45,728 --> 00:48:48,849
It's so good you wouldn't notice
if the person beside you dropped dead.

669
00:49:05,644 --> 00:49:06,677
Good, isn't it?

670
00:49:07,444 --> 00:49:08,677
Much better, right?

671
00:49:10,677 --> 00:49:11,711
Yes.

672
00:49:12,051 --> 00:49:13,971
See? I told you.

673
00:49:14,444 --> 00:49:16,311
Here's your spicy noodle soup.

674
00:49:18,144 --> 00:49:20,519
- One bowl of rice as well, please.
- Yes.

675
00:49:20,544 --> 00:49:22,044
- Enjoy your meal.
- Yes.

676
00:49:44,544 --> 00:49:45,577
This is the taste.

677
00:49:45,577 --> 00:49:47,123
- One bowl of rice.
- Yes.

678
00:49:55,911 --> 00:49:56,944
Here we go.

679
00:49:58,477 --> 00:50:00,854
This time we go for something even better.

680
00:50:02,544 --> 00:50:03,611
If you drop dead...

681
00:50:03,990 --> 00:50:06,410
from how good it is,
I can't be held responsible.

682
00:50:08,471 --> 00:50:09,644
There. Like this.

683
00:50:13,564 --> 00:50:14,944
What do you think you're doing?

684
00:50:16,311 --> 00:50:18,111
The spicy radish salad is one thing,

685
00:50:18,544 --> 00:50:20,444
but the true value
of the spicy noodle soup here,

686
00:50:20,671 --> 00:50:23,784
is when you stir white rice
right into the broth like this...

687
00:50:25,444 --> 00:50:26,511
Even so, how can you dump rice
into another person's noodles,

688
00:50:26,511 --> 00:50:28,944
without even asking?

689
00:50:30,325 --> 00:50:31,477
I...

690
00:50:31,844 --> 00:50:33,477
I just find it so delicious...

691
00:50:34,377 --> 00:50:37,386
and when people share a table,
you share even a grain of rice...

692
00:50:37,411 --> 00:50:40,203
Then stir in as much as you like
and eat it yourself.

693
00:50:41,744 --> 00:50:42,844
Look at this. Just look at it.

694
00:50:42,844 --> 00:50:44,411
It's like dog food.

695
00:50:45,111 --> 00:50:46,211
Honestly.

696
00:50:46,450 --> 00:50:48,385
What a strange man.

697
00:50:50,344 --> 00:50:51,477
Ma'am.

698
00:50:51,641 --> 00:50:52,911
Excuse me, ma'am.

699
00:51:00,811 --> 00:51:03,896
Is that something to get angry about?

700
00:51:04,477 --> 00:51:07,469
In this cold world,
wanting to share something good,

701
00:51:07,977 --> 00:51:09,044
is that so wrong?

702
00:51:13,124 --> 00:51:15,034
If dog food tastes this good,

703
00:51:15,190 --> 00:51:17,568
I'd happily eat it my whole life.

704
00:51:23,064 --> 00:51:24,574
It's delicious.

705
00:51:26,944 --> 00:51:28,820
It's like dog food.

706
00:51:30,144 --> 00:51:31,477
You should have taken me along.

707
00:51:31,677 --> 00:51:33,744
I was craving that place too.

708
00:51:33,770 --> 00:51:35,225
Isn't he out of his mind?

709
00:51:35,717 --> 00:51:36,750
Me?

710
00:51:38,744 --> 00:51:40,044
A complete stranger,

711
00:51:40,044 --> 00:51:41,777
stirring rice into my bowl
without even asking.

712
00:51:41,777 --> 00:51:43,079
Is that sane?

713
00:51:43,424 --> 00:51:45,953
Were they his noodles? They were mine.

714
00:51:48,308 --> 00:51:51,417
Who stirs rice into your noodles
without asking?

715
00:51:51,451 --> 00:51:53,944
I should have shoved his face
straight into the bowl...

716
00:51:53,944 --> 00:51:55,718
before I left.

717
00:51:55,777 --> 00:51:56,811
Though,

718
00:51:57,077 --> 00:52:00,244
stirring rice into the spicy noodle soup
there is honestly the real way to eat it.

719
00:52:00,292 --> 00:52:03,311
Do you think I don't know that?

720
00:52:03,611 --> 00:52:05,344
Dr. Jeong keeps going on and on,

721
00:52:05,344 --> 00:52:07,011
about watching my carbohydrates,

722
00:52:07,011 --> 00:52:08,811
so I hold back as much as I can.

723
00:52:10,411 --> 00:52:13,479
That place is such a hot spot
that all sorts of people go there.

724
00:52:14,177 --> 00:52:17,077
Just put it down to a strange
encounter and forget it.

725
00:52:17,877 --> 00:52:19,744
Getting worked up only hurts you.

726
00:52:20,777 --> 00:52:22,077
Honestly...

727
00:52:22,411 --> 00:52:24,977
It was my first proper meal in ages,

728
00:52:24,977 --> 00:52:26,622
and that man ruined all of it.

729
00:52:27,477 --> 00:52:28,611
And his face looked just like...

730
00:52:28,611 --> 00:52:31,144
a mouse that fell into vinegar.

731
00:52:31,977 --> 00:52:33,477
You're saying he was that cute?

732
00:52:33,502 --> 00:52:34,876
(Chairwoman Hong Ok Seon)

733
00:52:34,911 --> 00:52:35,944
Aren't you busy?

734
00:52:35,944 --> 00:52:37,111
Off you go. Get back to work.

735
00:52:56,270 --> 00:52:57,741
Who is it?

736
00:53:00,482 --> 00:53:02,022
Who's there?

737
00:53:04,051 --> 00:53:05,311
Jang Seo Hyeon.

738
00:53:07,249 --> 00:53:10,186
If you're home, come in.
Why are you standing there?

739
00:53:10,211 --> 00:53:12,084
Mom.

740
00:53:14,677 --> 00:53:15,944
Have you been drinking?

741
00:53:17,244 --> 00:53:20,054
Not much. Just a little.

742
00:53:24,077 --> 00:53:25,698
That isn't a little.

743
00:53:29,111 --> 00:53:30,311
What's wrong?

744
00:53:31,177 --> 00:53:32,844
Did something happen at work?

745
00:53:34,344 --> 00:53:36,077
Nothing happened at work,

746
00:53:38,684 --> 00:53:39,717
Mom.

747
00:53:39,916 --> 00:53:41,683
Should I just emigrate?

748
00:53:42,644 --> 00:53:43,644
What?

749
00:53:43,644 --> 00:53:44,744
Never mind.

750
00:53:44,944 --> 00:53:47,648
Why would I leave and make him happy?

751
00:53:48,826 --> 00:53:51,683
Kim Mu Jin, that awful man.

752
00:53:51,711 --> 00:53:54,550
That idiot, that complete fool.

753
00:53:56,977 --> 00:53:58,144
What's wrong?

754
00:53:59,111 --> 00:54:01,081
Why are you crying?

755
00:54:01,837 --> 00:54:03,521
Did Mu Jin say something to you?

756
00:54:04,777 --> 00:54:05,811
Mom.

757
00:54:06,211 --> 00:54:07,763
Am I really that unappealing?

758
00:54:07,977 --> 00:54:09,244
No.

759
00:54:09,244 --> 00:54:11,044
Why would you be unappealing?

760
00:54:12,511 --> 00:54:16,599
Why would you, the most precious
and beautiful girl in the world?

761
00:54:17,177 --> 00:54:19,044
Did Mu Jin say something like that to you?

762
00:54:20,011 --> 00:54:21,525
He didn't,

763
00:54:21,744 --> 00:54:23,111
but it feels that way.

764
00:54:23,644 --> 00:54:25,352
How else could he do this to me?

765
00:54:25,377 --> 00:54:28,344
He knows I like him and that I've waited
for him and no one else...

766
00:54:28,344 --> 00:54:33,518
So how does he waver the moment
that woman shows up again?

767
00:54:33,577 --> 00:54:34,644
That woman?

768
00:54:36,111 --> 00:54:37,177
Don't tell me...

769
00:54:37,644 --> 00:54:39,377
The one Mu Jin used to see...

770
00:54:39,377 --> 00:54:40,977
She's turned up again?

771
00:54:45,444 --> 00:54:49,344
This is why I told you not to see Mu Jin.

772
00:54:49,777 --> 00:54:51,469
What could you possibly lack?

773
00:54:51,530 --> 00:54:54,183
I raised you so well.

774
00:54:59,077 --> 00:55:01,711
He can't even recognize
how wonderful and beautiful you are...

775
00:55:01,711 --> 00:55:03,311
That boy does nothing but hurt you,

776
00:55:03,644 --> 00:55:05,677
and now I wouldn't take him
even if he came begging.

777
00:55:05,844 --> 00:55:08,177
Men a thousand times better looking
than Kim Mu Jin,

778
00:55:08,177 --> 00:55:11,411
finer, smarter, and kinder...

779
00:55:11,411 --> 00:55:13,344
Men who'd be crazy about you,

780
00:55:13,344 --> 00:55:15,244
I'll line them all up for you,

781
00:55:15,444 --> 00:55:17,644
so you just kick someone
like Kim Mu Jin to the curb.

782
00:55:18,077 --> 00:55:21,083
If that were easy, I wouldn't
have spent 23 years like this.

783
00:55:23,814 --> 00:55:25,044
Jang Seo Hyeon.

784
00:55:25,877 --> 00:55:29,601
Why are you doing this to me?

785
00:55:31,804 --> 00:55:33,344
Don't tell Dad.

786
00:55:33,644 --> 00:55:34,744
I'm going to wash up.

787
00:55:36,658 --> 00:55:37,911
Seo Hyeon.

788
00:55:42,444 --> 00:55:43,777
That wretched boy.

789
00:55:50,444 --> 00:55:52,877
(Jeong Woo)

790
00:55:57,111 --> 00:55:59,544
Hello, Jeong Woo. It's Seo Hyeon's mother.

791
00:56:00,477 --> 00:56:02,244
That girl Mu Jin used to see,

792
00:56:02,244 --> 00:56:03,777
I hear she's turned up again?

793
00:56:04,377 --> 00:56:06,511
What sort of girl is she?
What does she do?

794
00:56:07,477 --> 00:56:09,567
And what do her parents do?

795
00:56:12,676 --> 00:56:15,978
Instead of only pressing Mu Jin,
I think I need to meet her myself.

796
00:56:16,777 --> 00:56:18,411
I'm simply curious.

797
00:56:18,411 --> 00:56:21,411
Just what is so remarkable
about her compared to my Seo Hyeon,

798
00:56:21,577 --> 00:56:23,777
that I need to see and confirm
it with my own eyes.

799
00:56:25,105 --> 00:56:28,111
You know that girl's name
and phone number, don't you?

800
00:56:36,377 --> 00:56:38,111
(Dad)

801
00:56:43,244 --> 00:56:45,644
Dad, unless it's urgent,
I'll call you back later.

802
00:56:45,777 --> 00:56:47,811
It is urgent. Very urgent.

803
00:56:48,211 --> 00:56:50,544
Gyu Yeong is going after the twins.

804
00:56:50,811 --> 00:56:52,911
So come and stop her, Gyu Rim.

805
00:56:54,377 --> 00:56:57,144
You scold Gyu Yeong yourself
and tell her to stop.

806
00:56:57,248 --> 00:56:59,328
Does she listen to me?

807
00:56:59,457 --> 00:57:01,194
She treats me like a barking dog.

808
00:57:01,611 --> 00:57:03,677
I'm afraid the sparks
will land on me too...

809
00:57:03,844 --> 00:57:05,977
I'm calling from the rooftop myself.

810
00:57:06,011 --> 00:57:07,211
Isn't Gyu O there either?

811
00:57:07,377 --> 00:57:09,559
He isn't. So hurry up and come.

812
00:57:09,777 --> 00:57:11,077
It's an emergency.

813
00:57:11,077 --> 00:57:12,111
Maximum Alert.

814
00:57:17,744 --> 00:57:19,642
What are you going to do about this?

815
00:57:20,657 --> 00:57:21,892
I'll take responsibility.

816
00:57:22,411 --> 00:57:23,911
How exactly will you do that?

817
00:57:24,044 --> 00:57:25,411
Do you even know what this cost?

818
00:57:25,557 --> 00:57:28,379
This is a limited edition
they don't even sell anymore.

819
00:57:29,238 --> 00:57:30,617
Did Gyu Seo do it on purpose?

820
00:57:31,111 --> 00:57:32,811
If the clothes are that precious,

821
00:57:32,811 --> 00:57:34,777
you should keep them out
of the family laundry,

822
00:57:35,044 --> 00:57:36,611
or at least have them dry-cleaned.

823
00:57:37,570 --> 00:57:40,572
You can't even manage your own things,
yet you throw a fit over the laundry.

824
00:57:43,211 --> 00:57:44,277
"You?"

825
00:57:44,477 --> 00:57:45,511
Hey.

826
00:57:45,577 --> 00:57:46,944
Did you just say "you?"

827
00:57:46,944 --> 00:57:48,460
Yes, I did.

828
00:57:49,211 --> 00:57:52,711
You call Gyu Rim "hey" and "you"
every single day, so why not?

829
00:57:52,944 --> 00:57:54,951
- Why can't I?
- Gyu Min.

830
00:57:55,344 --> 00:57:56,577
You don't even think of me,

831
00:57:56,877 --> 00:57:59,211
or Gyu Seo, as your siblings anyway.

832
00:57:59,277 --> 00:58:01,500
- This little...
- Gyu Yeong.

833
00:58:04,044 --> 00:58:06,211
Fine. If you want to pull hair, pull mine,

834
00:58:06,211 --> 00:58:07,711
and if you want to rage, rage at me.

835
00:58:07,711 --> 00:58:08,911
Leave Gyu Seo out of it.

836
00:58:09,011 --> 00:58:10,811
Go on, pull it all out.

837
00:58:10,944 --> 00:58:13,011
Do you want to die? Hey!

838
00:58:13,444 --> 00:58:14,944
What are you doing?

839
00:58:15,683 --> 00:58:17,717
Let go. Let go of her now.

840
00:58:21,177 --> 00:58:22,344
What do you think you're doing?

841
00:58:22,744 --> 00:58:24,111
Why are you laying hands on Gyu Min?

842
00:58:24,311 --> 00:58:25,877
Who are you to lay hands on a her?

843
00:58:25,877 --> 00:58:27,777
If you don't know,
keep quiet and stay out of it.

844
00:58:27,944 --> 00:58:29,111
It was my fault.

845
00:58:29,377 --> 00:58:31,711
I was trying to finish the laundry
before you got home,

846
00:58:31,944 --> 00:58:33,777
and Gyu Yeong's clothes
must have gotten mixed in.

847
00:58:34,544 --> 00:58:37,077
It's a piece she treasures,
and it stained badly...

848
00:58:37,077 --> 00:58:38,911
Even so, why grab her by the hair?

849
00:58:39,284 --> 00:58:42,480
How many times have I told you
to wash your clothes separately?

850
00:58:43,044 --> 00:58:46,011
You made the mistake,
so who are you taking it out on?

851
00:58:51,311 --> 00:58:52,611
This.

852
00:58:54,377 --> 00:58:56,977
feel even worse?
It's exactly like those twins.

853
00:58:57,777 --> 00:58:59,768
The things I like,
the things I treasure...

854
00:59:00,777 --> 00:59:02,777
The moment they get involved,
it all ends up ruined like this.

855
00:59:03,581 --> 00:59:07,911
You two feel like stains
splashed across my life. It's revolting.

856
00:59:07,911 --> 00:59:08,944
Han Gyu Yeong.

857
00:59:09,644 --> 00:59:10,811
Watch your mouth.

858
00:59:10,811 --> 00:59:12,411
If it weren't for them in the first place,

859
00:59:14,411 --> 00:59:16,744
if it weren't for their mother,
our mom wouldn't have divorced,

860
00:59:16,744 --> 00:59:18,377
we wouldn't have been left behind,

861
00:59:18,582 --> 00:59:20,811
and this house wouldn't have fallen
apart like this...

862
00:59:20,923 --> 00:59:22,723
I said watch your mouth.

863
00:59:23,311 --> 00:59:24,311
You two go inside.

864
00:59:24,311 --> 00:59:25,944
Gyu Yeong has completely lost her mind.

865
00:59:25,944 --> 00:59:27,444
There's no reason to listen
to someone who's lost it.

866
00:59:27,444 --> 00:59:29,144
- Go inside, quickly.
- Hey!

867
00:59:29,144 --> 00:59:31,677
- Let's go in.
- Let go. Say more, go on.

868
00:59:31,811 --> 00:59:32,844
Gyu Min.

869
00:59:33,044 --> 00:59:34,211
Stay inside, Gyu Min.

870
00:59:34,517 --> 00:59:35,917
I'll take care of all of it.

871
00:59:37,411 --> 00:59:38,911
Whose side are you on?

872
00:59:39,044 --> 00:59:41,311
If you're taking a side,
it should be mine.

873
00:59:41,877 --> 00:59:43,344
We're sisters from the same mother,

874
00:59:43,344 --> 00:59:45,177
and those two are the children
of our sworn enemy.

875
00:59:45,311 --> 00:59:46,711
Shut your mouth, Han Gyu Yeong.

876
00:59:48,211 --> 00:59:49,311
Han Gyu Rim.

877
00:59:50,544 --> 00:59:52,653
You really are beyond saving.

878
00:59:52,777 --> 00:59:54,711
I thought you could be fixed and used,

879
00:59:54,711 --> 00:59:57,144
but now I see you're garbage
that can't even be recycled.

880
00:59:57,611 --> 00:59:58,644
Han Gyu Rim.

881
00:59:58,777 --> 01:00:00,886
- Get out of this house. Now.
- Hey!

882
01:00:00,911 --> 01:00:04,042
Dad, I don't have a sister like this,

883
01:00:04,190 --> 01:00:06,741
so strike this girl from our family
register right now.

884
01:00:08,444 --> 01:00:11,477
I'll be struck from it the moment
I marry anyway, so don't worry.

885
01:00:11,477 --> 01:00:12,711
Right now.

886
01:00:12,977 --> 01:00:14,477
Get out right now.

887
01:00:16,098 --> 01:00:19,078
I can't stand the sight of you
for one more second, so go.

888
01:00:19,544 --> 01:00:21,386
You think I can't leave
because you told me to?

889
01:00:21,577 --> 01:00:24,378
I don't want to spend one more second
in this miserable house either.

890
01:00:30,811 --> 01:00:31,844
Gyu Rim.

891
01:00:39,417 --> 01:00:41,553
Shall I get you water? Do you want water?

892
01:00:42,350 --> 01:00:44,547
No, shall I get you a drink? Want one?

893
01:00:45,744 --> 01:00:46,911
No, I...

894
01:00:46,911 --> 01:00:48,511
I came here from work
and I have to go back.

895
01:00:48,904 --> 01:00:49,937
All right.

896
01:00:55,977 --> 01:00:57,477
When I get home from work,

897
01:00:57,711 --> 01:01:00,144
I'd love the spicy rice cakes
you make, Gyu Min.

898
01:01:00,677 --> 01:01:01,711
Could you make them for me?

899
01:01:03,911 --> 01:01:06,077
Yes, as many as you want.

900
01:01:07,377 --> 01:01:09,044
Thank you for doing the laundry, Gyu Seo.

901
01:01:09,544 --> 01:01:12,211
You're the only one who ever
runs a load thinking of me.

902
01:01:13,311 --> 01:01:14,511
It's nothing.

903
01:01:22,111 --> 01:01:23,344
I'm the one to blame.

904
01:01:25,277 --> 01:01:26,277
Next.

905
01:01:26,277 --> 01:01:27,277
Summer, winter.

906
01:01:27,277 --> 01:01:28,744
One, two, three.

907
01:01:28,744 --> 01:01:29,777
- Winter.
- Winter.

908
01:01:32,144 --> 01:01:33,978
- You like winter?
- Yes.

909
01:01:34,852 --> 01:01:38,318
That's seven questions so far,
and all seven have matched.

910
01:01:38,351 --> 01:01:39,384
Exactly.

911
01:01:41,977 --> 01:01:44,677
Have you ever taken
that MBTI test by any chance?

912
01:01:45,044 --> 01:01:46,744
Yes. Let's do this one
at the same time too.

913
01:01:46,744 --> 01:01:48,744
All right. One, two, three.

914
01:01:48,744 --> 01:01:50,011
- ISFJ.
- ISFJ.

915
01:01:50,944 --> 01:01:51,944
ISFJ?

916
01:01:52,411 --> 01:01:54,011
IS, ISFJ.

917
01:01:54,011 --> 01:01:55,244
So that's how you say it.

918
01:01:56,577 --> 01:01:59,373
But sometimes I get a "T"
for the third letter.

919
01:01:59,677 --> 01:02:01,211
You too?

920
01:02:01,211 --> 01:02:03,738
Same here. When I'm studying,
things like that.

921
01:02:04,577 --> 01:02:06,611
For me it's when I'm working...

922
01:02:07,744 --> 01:02:09,311
and when I have to face
someone I don't like.

923
01:02:09,423 --> 01:02:11,151
Amazing. Me too.

924
01:02:11,491 --> 01:02:14,311
We're completely in sync.

925
01:02:17,311 --> 01:02:19,321
What is this? We're completely in sync.

926
01:02:32,111 --> 01:02:35,044
I caught on right away.

927
01:02:35,544 --> 01:02:36,844
That's right.

928
01:02:37,011 --> 01:02:40,544
Even within Jeollado, the southern part
has a different flavor.

929
01:02:41,844 --> 01:02:42,977
It certainly does.

930
01:02:43,044 --> 01:02:44,677
You catch on at once.

931
01:02:46,211 --> 01:02:47,811
Where's your hometown, ma'am?

932
01:02:47,811 --> 01:02:48,877
Mine is around Wando.

933
01:02:48,877 --> 01:02:50,477
Wando?

934
01:02:50,744 --> 01:02:52,211
Mine is around Jindo.

935
01:02:52,377 --> 01:02:55,011
Wando is Heung Sik's father's side.

936
01:02:55,377 --> 01:02:58,611
Though we moved to Busan
as soon as Heung Sik was born.

937
01:02:58,711 --> 01:03:01,311
No wonder. It all clicked into place.

938
01:03:01,544 --> 01:03:04,211
The moment I tasted these dishes at lunch,

939
01:03:04,344 --> 01:03:06,617
I thought of my own mother.

940
01:03:07,677 --> 01:03:09,411
That's why the moment I finished work,

941
01:03:09,411 --> 01:03:12,677
I came here with the receipt
and the plastic bag in hand.

942
01:03:13,077 --> 01:03:16,077
Hold on. Of them all,
which was the most delicious?

943
01:03:18,031 --> 01:03:20,616
How could anyone pick just one?

944
01:03:21,277 --> 01:03:22,444
Well...

945
01:03:22,444 --> 01:03:26,544
If I really had to choose one,

946
01:03:26,544 --> 01:03:28,044
the spicy skate salad?

947
01:03:28,911 --> 01:03:30,681
What am I to do?

948
01:03:30,877 --> 01:03:33,276
That one has sold out.

949
01:03:33,877 --> 01:03:36,977
I'd happily whip up
another batch if I could,

950
01:03:36,977 --> 01:03:39,111
but I'm not the one who made it.

951
01:03:39,411 --> 01:03:44,446
That spicy skate salad only tastes right
when Gyeol's mother makes it.

952
01:03:44,711 --> 01:03:46,119
Gyeol's mother?

953
01:03:47,220 --> 01:03:48,811
Is she your daughter-in-law?

954
01:03:49,411 --> 01:03:54,086
- Mother and daughter-in-law both gifted?
- No.

955
01:03:54,111 --> 01:03:56,643
She isn't my daughter-in-law,

956
01:03:56,877 --> 01:03:59,711
though she might be one day...

957
01:04:00,177 --> 01:04:02,311
If that happened, I'd be delighted.

958
01:04:02,544 --> 01:04:06,494
But that's nothing more
than a wish of my own.

959
01:04:09,211 --> 01:04:11,577
There she is, my wish.

960
01:04:12,777 --> 01:04:13,811
You're back?

961
01:04:17,644 --> 01:04:18,677
Gyu Rim.

962
01:04:23,244 --> 01:04:25,367
- Mu Jin.
- Yes.

963
01:04:27,411 --> 01:04:28,807
You know my mom well, don't you?

964
01:04:31,244 --> 01:04:32,277
Back then...

965
01:04:32,511 --> 01:04:33,977
Eight years ago,

966
01:04:34,711 --> 01:04:36,377
you met my mom, didn't you?

967
01:04:47,144 --> 01:04:48,444
I knew it.

968
01:04:50,544 --> 01:04:52,291
Were you and my mom in love?

969
01:05:28,675 --> 01:05:31,319
(Love on the Menu)

970
01:05:31,344 --> 01:05:34,111
Because I'd like to have a dad now too.

971
01:05:34,144 --> 01:05:36,277
You have no right to come crashing
into Han Gyu Rim's life like this,

972
01:05:36,277 --> 01:05:38,611
and turn it upside down.

973
01:05:39,277 --> 01:05:40,911
Just buy it from another shop.

974
01:05:41,344 --> 01:05:42,344
Just sell it to me.

975
01:05:42,344 --> 01:05:43,644
Gyu Yeong, what are you doing?

976
01:05:43,911 --> 01:05:45,244
Please help me, Chairman.

977
01:05:45,269 --> 01:05:46,786
What sort of person is he?

978
01:05:46,811 --> 01:05:48,777
He's someone I'd really like
to be close with.

979
01:05:48,972 --> 01:05:52,619
If you say that about him,
I'd better make a good impression too.

980
01:05:52,644 --> 01:05:54,213
I think today...

981
01:05:54,364 --> 01:05:57,044
I saw Mu Jin's son, Mom.

982
01:05:57,444 --> 01:05:58,519
What?

983
01:06:01,675 --> 01:06:03,675
Dramaday.me
